cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Q-OMICS or the cohort it assembles, please cite this software and the underlying data."
title: "Q-OMICS: a hybrid quantum-classical foundation model for multi-omics biomarker discovery"
abstract: >-
  Q-OMICS is an open-source pipeline that combines a fidelity quantum kernel
  with a cross-omic transformer to rank molecular biomarkers for early-stage
  cancer detection. It assembles genome, transcriptome and proteome layers
  from public TCGA archives, cross-validates the hybrid model against a full
  set of classical baselines, reports the geometric difference between the
  quantum and classical kernels, and emits a pathway-annotated biomarker
  panel with effect sizes and false-discovery-rate control.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shreyasderaje/Q-OMICS"
